(Epoxy Cure Oven Specification Rev 4.2) Tj
T* (Warmup ramp region: use consecutive segments with both endpoints between 60 C and 120 C.) Tj
T* (Maximum warmup ramp: 1.40 C/min.) Tj
T* (Effective cure hold: count only time between 150 C and 162 C using linear interpolation at both boundaries.) Tj
T* (Batch effective hold is the minimum hold across all embedded thermocouples.) Tj
T* (Release window for effective hold: 600 s to 840 s inclusive.) Tj
T* (Peak overshoot is max\(0, hottest peak - target_peak_c from batch log\).) Tj
T* (Release overshoot limit: 3.0 C. Rebake overshoot limit: 1.5 C.) Tj
T* (Peak uniformity is hottest peak minus coolest peak across the batch. Limit: 4.0 C.) Tj
T* (Disposition logic:) Tj
T* (1. release when ramp, hold, overshoot, uniformity all pass and door_open_alarm = 0.) Tj
T* (2. rebake only when the only thermal failure is short hold, rebake_allowed = yes, rebake_count = 0, door_open_alarm = 0, and overshoot/uniformity still meet rebake limits.) Tj
T* (3. otherwise hold.) Tj
T* (Reason code order: warmup_ramp_high, effective_hold_short, effective_hold_long, peak_overshoot_high, uniformity_exceeds_limit, door_open_alarm, rebake_not_allowed.) Tj
T* (Rebake profile code: RBK-150C-12M.) Tj
